# Context

## Why This Way
Phase 2's contract assumed a T073 change to evaluate, but T072 selected
no Phase 1 candidate, so T073 closed empty and there was nothing to
accept or discard. The matrix was still repeated at the integrated HEAD
because production code had moved since the T070 baseline (the T075
hub-restart transport fix); the repetition confirms the T072 budgets
describe the shipped tree rather than comparing a candidate.

## Gotchas
- Steady p95 straddles the 2 s target on single runs (1.971/2.014 s here,
  1.945/1.999 s in T070): a 1,000-sample draw moves p95 by more than the
  margin. Do not read one side of the line as a regression; the p99 < 2.5 s
  companion target is the stable check.
- The mixed-read/write WAL high-water mark read 33-65 MiB against the
  27-32 MiB T070 basis (one run 1 MiB over the 64 MiB ceiling, inside the
  allowed +/-50%). The basis was a low draw; the mark races
  auto-checkpoints against reader snapshots.

